#: ../../../driver-api/infrastructure:36: ../drivers/base/core.c:4575
msgid ""
"given that some subsystems (networking and infiniband) use this function, "
"with no immediate plans for this to change, we cannot assume or require that "
"this function not be called at all."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/infrastructure:36: ../drivers/base/core.c:4579
msgid ""
"However, if you're writing new code, do not call this function. The "
"following text from Kay Sievers offers some insight:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/infrastructure:36: ../drivers/base/core.c:4582
msgid ""
"Renaming devices is racy at many levels, symlinks and other stuff are not "
"replaced atomically, and you get a \"move\" uevent, but it's not easy to "
"connect the event to the old and new device. Device nodes are not renamed at "
"all, there isn't even support for that in the kernel now."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/infrastructure:36: ../drivers/base/core.c:4587
msgid ""
"In the meantime, during renaming, your target name might be taken by another "
"driver, creating conflicts. Or the old name is taken directly after you "
"renamed it -- then you get events for the same DEVPATH, before you even see "
"the \"move\" event. It's just a mess, and nothing new should ever rely on "
"kernel device renaming. Besides that, it's not even implemented now for "
"other things than (driver-core wise very simple) network devices."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../driver-api/infrastructure:36: ../drivers/base/core.c:4594
msgid ""
"Make up a \"real\" name in the driver before you register anything, or add "
"some other attributes for userspace to find the device, or use udev to add "
"symlinks -- but never rename kernel devices later, it's a complete mess. We "
"don't even want to get into that and try to implement the missing pieces in "
"the core. We really have other pieces to fix in the driver core mess. :)"
msgstr ""

